## Which kinds of sources do AI Overviews cite, by sector? {% #citation-types %}

Citation collection required one API call per query, so pulling every AI-Overview-positive query in the panel was not practical. The citation sample was instead drawn with a predeclared stratified random rule: up to 10 AI-Overview-positive queries per sector, selected with a fixed random seed (Python's `random.seed(20260925)` over each sector's sorted query list), giving 100 queries, exactly 10 per sector. This replaces a top-by-volume selection: each eligible query within a sector had an equal chance of selection. 3 of the 100 sampled queries returned an AI Overview with no external sitelinks. The other 97 queries returned 411 individual citation rows, with 17 (4.1%) left unresolved because Google returned an opaque redirect link instead of a readable URL.

| Sector | Resolved citations | Government/NHS/public body | Publisher/media | Brand/company | Forum/UGC | Reference | Other | Unresolved |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Health/NHS | 47 | 25 | 2 | 12 | 1 | 2 | 5 | 6 |
| Finance/Banking | 27 | 3 | 6 | 15 | 2 | 1 | 0 | 2 |
| Legal | 34 | 9 | 1 | 14 | 1 | 4 | 5 | 6 |
| Travel/Tourism | 34 | 8 | 0 | 21 | 5 | 0 | 0 | 2 |
| Home Improvement/Trades | 39 | 0 | 1 | 33 | 4 | 1 | 0 | 1 |
| Retail/Ecommerce | 32 | 0 | 2 | 28 | 0 | 2 | 0 | 0 |
| Automotive | 50 | 1 | 5 | 38 | 5 | 1 | 0 | 0 |
| Education | 50 | 14 | 2 | 28 | 4 | 2 | 0 | 0 |
| Food/Restaurants | 32 | 2 | 10 | 11 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 0 |
| Insurance | 49 | 1 | 4 | 41 | 3 | 0 | 0 | 0 |
| **All sectors** | **394** | **63** | **33** | **241** | **29** | **17** | **11** | **17** |

{% chart type="donut" eyebrow="Citation type, 100-query stratified sample" title="Source types among 394 resolved citation rows in this sample, 25 September 2026" data="Brand/company:61.2|Government/NHS/public body:16.0|Publisher/media:8.4|Forum/UGC:7.4|Reference:4.3|Other:2.8" suffix="%" source="Ahrefs GB SERP data, 100-query stratified citation sample" /%}

Government, NHS and public-body sources are strongest in Health/NHS (25 of 47, 53%, dominated by nhs.uk and gov.uk pages) and roughly equal in Legal and Education (9 of 34, 26%, and 14 of 50, 28%: gov.uk guidance on divorce, wills, probate and apprenticeships, and the National Careers Service). Brand/company citations account for 76.0% to 87.5% of resolved citations in Automotive, Home Improvement/Trades, Insurance and Retail/Ecommerce, driven by price-comparison sites (Compare the Market, MoneySuperMarket, GoCompare) and product/service sellers, with close to zero government or reference citations in those four sectors. Food/Restaurants has the highest publisher share among the sampled sectors (10 of 32, 31%, recipe and nutrition publishers such as BBC Good Food and Healthline), close behind its own brand/company share (11 of 32, 34%).

The most-cited individual domains, pooled across all resolved citations, were gov.uk (26), youtube.com (20), moneysavingexpert.com (15), comparethemarket.com (15) and moneysupermarket.com (14). This reflects one snapshot of one 100-query stratified sample, not a ranked market-share table. Every sector contributed exactly 10 queries to the citation sample, so a sector's resolved-citation total in the table above varies with how many sitelinks its 10 sampled queries happened to return, not with that sector's panel size.

